                     <mods:roleTerm type="text">institution</mods:roleTerm>
                  </mods:role>
                  <mods:namePart>Universidade de Araraquara – UNIARA</mods:namePart>
               </mods:name>
               <mods:extension>
                  <mods:dateAccessioned encoding="iso8601">2018-12-11T17:08:18Z</mods:dateAccessioned>
               </mods:extension>
               <mods:extension>
                  <mods:dateAvailable encoding="iso8601">2018-12-11T17:08:18Z</mods:dateAvailable>
               </mods:extension>
               <mods:originInfo>
                  <mods:dateIssued encoding="iso8601">2017-02-10</mods:dateIssued>
               </mods:originInfo>
               <mods:identifier type="none"/>
               <mods:identifier type="citation">Carbohydrate Polymers, v. 157, p. 1013-1023.</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="issn">0144-86171879-1344</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="uri">http://hdl.handle.net/11449/173909</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="doi">10.1016/j.carbpol.2016.10.062</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="scopus">2-s2.0-85005950342</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="file">2-s2.0-85005950342.pdf</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="orcid">0000-0002-6273-86120000-0003-0988-29700000-0001-9081-24130000-0003-0221-22880000-0003-3020-92380000-0001-9284-2819</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="dimensions">pub.1022812026</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="pmid">27987801</mods:identifier>
               <mods:abstract>Although resistant starch/pectin (RS/P) films have previously displayed suitable properties for colon-specific drug delivery, nanocomposite films were developed aiming to enhance physicochemical, thermal, mechanical and barrier properties, as well as the low oral bioavailability of methotrexate (MTX). FEG-SEM micrographs of nanocomposite films showed different interaction patterns occurring among nanocellulose and RS/P. The nanofiller addition led to an increase in the thermal stability, probably due to its interaction with RS crystalline double helices. Results also displayed an improvement of the puncture strength, while barrier properties revealed a low water vapor permeability. Ex vivo bioadhesion test displayed the nanocomposites films to interact strongly with porcine gastrointestinal mucosa. In vitro drug release studies showed that the films developed enhanced the drug dissolution rates with approximately 80% of MTX release in 150 min, suggesting the potential of these materials as a poor solubility drugs carrier, which constitutes an important tool for enhancing oral bioavailability.</mods:abstract>
               <mods:language>
                  <mods:languageTerm authority="rfc3066">eng</mods:languageTerm>
               </mods:language>
               <mods:accessCondition type="useAndReproduction"/>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Cellulose nanofiber</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Free-standing films</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Methotrexate</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Nanocellulose</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Pectin</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:subject>
                  <mods:topic>Resistant starch</mods:topic>
               </mods:subject>
               <mods:titleInfo>
                  <mods:title>Resistant starch/pectin free-standing films reinforced with nanocellulose intended for colonic methotrexate release</mods:title>
               </mods:titleInfo>
               <mods:genre>Artigo</mods:genre>
            </mods:mods>
         </xmlData>
      </mdWrap>
   </dmdSec>
