               <mods:identifier type="none"/>
               <mods:identifier type="citation">Proceedings of the 23rd Lake Louise Winter Institute: Fundamental Interactions, LLWI 2008, p. 328-332.</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="isbn">978-981-4280-93-8978-981-4280-94-5</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="uri">http://hdl.handle.net/11449/227400</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="doi">10.1142/9789814280945_0044</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="scopus">2-s2.0-84890961049</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="orcid">0000-0001-5384-28910000-0002-0474-1362</mods:identifier>
               <mods:identifier type="dimensions">pub.1096068847</mods:identifier>
               <mods:abstract>We analyze non-rclativistic Limits of Podolsky generalized electrodynamics in the context of the 5-dimensional Galilean formalism. The &amp;apos;electric&amp;apos; and &amp;apos;magnetic&amp;apos; limits are studied in analogy with the work of Le Bellac and Levy-Leblond (1973). © 2009 World Scientific Publishing Co. Pte. Ltd.</mods:abstract>
